# Thesis context

## Topic
Bias in ML credit scoring and bias mitigation (pre-, in-, and post-processing). Application: Home Credit Default Risk ([Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/home-credit-default-risk)). Written thesis and presentation are deliverables; internal validation only — no Kaggle submission.

## Dataset
- Single dataset: all Home Credit CSVs in `data/`, linked at `SK_ID_CURR` / `SK_ID_PREV` / `SK_ID_BUREAU`.
- Target: `TARGET` (loan default). Column meanings: `data/HomeCredit_columns_description.csv`.
- Protected attributes: `CODE_GENDER` (mandatory); intersectionality via gender × `DAYS_BIRTH`.
- **Include** protected attributes in model features.

## Pipeline (not two competing models)
- `analysis/notebooks/` — **EDA** (notebooks per table/domain; scripts/modules for shared helpers and heavy jobs). Separate from model implementation.
- `src/` = **Feature engineering** across all tables, then **credit scoring model** (LightGBM on engineered features).
- **Goal:** one credit scorer built from all relational tables → fairness audit → mitigation. Performance is nice-to-have, not an RQ.

## Fairness work (not yet implemented)
- Metrics (default): demographic parity, equal opportunity, equalized odds; worst-group disparity over gender×age.
- Mitigation: one technique per stage (pre/in/post) — exact methods TBD.
- Use out-of-fold predictions for fairness evaluation. Watch small intersectional cell counts.

## Repo conventions
- All repo text in English unless explicitly told otherwise.
- Data and outputs gitignored; paths: `data/`